      "text": "Given that $f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2 \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)$\n\nReplace $x$ by $1 - x$ to obtain:\n\n\\[f(1 - x) + 2f(x) = 3(1 - x)^2 \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (2)\\]\n\nMultiply equation $(2)$ by $- \\frac{1}{2}.$  Then add to equation $(1).$\n\n\\[f(x) + 2f(1 - x) + -\\frac{1}{2}f(x) -f(x) = 3x^2 - \\frac{1}{2} (1 - x)^2 \\] \n\nSimplifying, we have\n\n\\[f(x) + f(1 - x) = 3x^2 - \\frac{1}{2} (1 - 2x + x^2) =  \\boxed{3x^2 - \\frac{1}{2} + x}. \\]\nThe answer is: 3x^2-\\frac{1}{2}+x",
