      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find \\( f(3) \\), we will follow a step-by-step substitution process to create a system of equations that allows us to isolate \\( f(3) \\).\n\n1. Start with the given functional equation:\n   \\[\n   f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2 \\quad \\text{for all } x\n   \\]\n\n2. Substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n   \\[\n   f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3 \\cdot 3^2\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   f(3) = 27 - 2f(-2) \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the original equation:\n   \\[\n   f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3 \\cdot (-2)^2\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   2f(3) + f(-2) = 12 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Substitute Equation 1 into Equation 2:\n   \\[\n   2(27 - 2f(-2)) + f(-2) = 12\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   54 - 4f(-2) + f(-2) = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   54 - 3f(-2) = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3f(-2) = 42\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(-2) = 14\n   \\]\n\n5. Substitute \\( f(-2) = 14 \\) back into Equation 2:\n   \\[\n   2f(3) + 14 = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2f(3) = -2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   f(3) = -1\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is\n\\[\n\\boxed{-1}\n\\]",
